member.summary:
            A custom method, by its  (exact, case included):


query: lists records with the query as a JSON body: where, order, select, paging, includeTotalCount;

insertMany: inserts the records of a JSON array;

updateMany: changes every record a where selects: { "where": {…}, "input": {…} };

deleteMany: deletes every record a where selects: { "where": {…} }; soft unless the query has hardDelete=true.

            Any other verb is a 400 UNKNOWN_METHOD problem, and runs nothing; it is written to the request log, as the
            action runs only for a request that bound.

Answers in the gateway's problem shape ({ type, title, status, code, detail, errors?, traceId }) wherever the framework would answer in its own, for the actions of the controller it is on and for no other controller:
a model-binding failure (an empty or malformed body, a query value that is not a bool) is a 400 VALIDATION_ERROR; this runs ahead of the one [ApiController] adds, so that one never answers;
a body that is not application/json (a missing content type, which [Consumes] refuses in the action pipeline) is a 415 UNSUPPORTED_MEDIA_TYPE; a wrong one is refused earlier, by the router, and gives that the same body;
an exception goes through ; a body over the size limit is a 413 PAYLOAD_TOO_LARGE and any other unreadable body a 400.

Gives the empty answers the router gives under the REST routes (/api/gateway/{entity}…) the gateway's problem body:
415: a POST, PATCH or PUT with a content type other than application/json never reaches the controller: the [Consumes] metadata makes the router refuse it, before any filter could answer. No action ran, so this also writes the request-log entry (spec 2026-11-04 §4);
404 NOT_FOUND: no route matches the path, e.g. an old /item URL or an entity name no schema can have (spec 2026-11-04 §3.3, §3.4);
405 METHOD_NOT_ALLOWED: the path exists but not for this method, e.g. PATCH /{entity}; the router's Allow header is kept.
An answer that already has a body (the service's own problems) is left as it is. The GraphQL endpoint (/api/gateway itself) and every other route are left as they are.

